-- R19 - Expression table: up to four expressions of each live view, the best one carded; alternates shadowed by theme;
-- arithmetic-only rejections printed as standing views (both Macro Takeaways digests).
-- Owner approval, 10 Nov 2026 (workflow review, decision 6: print an expression table for each theme, tag rejected
-- alternates by theme, no change to the gate).
-- Proposed 10 Nov 2026 with dash.propose_rule; apply_after = Sun 15 Nov 2026 20:00 SGT unless "oppose R19".
-- Body, title, rationale and revert_if below are byte-identical to the DB row (body md5 fae1305d9807f4ca39e7fa66e4d10c80);
-- the evidence is generalised (the DB copy carries counts and results from the book; this repo is public).
-- No code goes with it: the alternates use the shadow book as it is (shadow.record keeps any letter and the reason text),
-- and the weekly review reads them back by the "alt Pnn:" tag.
-- To put it in force before the Sunday window (one line in the Supabase SQL editor, project diiwqbxyhtgvozhncoef):
--   update dash.rules set status = 'in_force', decided_at = now(), apply_after = now() where rid = 'R19' and status = 'proposed';
select dash.propose_rule($j${"scope": "both", "title": "Expression table: up to four expressions of each live view, the best one carded; alternates shadowed by theme; arithmetic-only rejections printed as standing views", "body": "EXPRESSION TABLE (owner, 10 Nov 2026). THE TRADE TEST has judged one expression per lean, the first proxy named, so a live view with poor levels on that proxy was dropped and a view carded on its obvious proxy was never compared with a better one. From now a live view is tested in up to four expressions and the best is carded. The gate is unchanged: every part of THE TRADE TEST, EV > 0, the thin-edge line, R08, R09, R14 and R17 apply to each expression as to any candidate. Applies in both books.\n\n1. WHICH VIEWS. A candidate lean whose view passes test (d) (a reason it works now) and test (e) (priced no or partly). Those two tests judge the view, not the instrument, and are made once per lean. A lean that fails either is recorded in TESTED as today, on one expression, with no table.\n\n2. THE ROWS. Name the expressions first, before any number is computed; then run each through tests (a), (b), (c) and (f) with its own numbers written down as SHOW THE WORK requires: proxy, REF, stop, target, r/r, p beside p0, EV. Up to four, real alternatives only, never padded:\n(1) the natural linear proxy, as today;\n(2) a cross or relative-value form that isolates the driver: a cross in place of a dollar pair, a curve or spread in place of an outright, one market against its peer, on any proxy the spec allows, \"A-B\" and \"A/B\" included;\n(3) the option form: the R01 structure he would use (digital, one-touch or spread), priced and gated exactly as R01 prices a convexity card;\n(4) another market that carries the same view: the equity or rates leg of an FX view, an Asian-hours proxy under R17 item 4, the other end of a pass-through.\nRows of one view share its story. Each row's p is the chance that its own target prints before its own stop, and it differs from row (1)'s p only for a reason the row states in 6 words or fewer (nearer levels, carry, a noisier second leg). R01's \"a lean is tested once a day, in one class only\" gives way to this table and to nothing else: the option row is named with the others, before any number.\n\n3. WHICH ROW IS CARDED. The row with the highest EV among those that pass every part; rows within 0.05R of each other go to the lower-numbered row. One card per view. Two limits. (i) While R18's twin trial runs, on a single FX proxy a linear row that passes is carded ahead of the option row whatever their EVs, because its TWIN line already scores the option beside it; the option row is carded there only when no linear row passes. (ii) R01's scope and its cap of 5 convexity cards stand. If no row passes, nothing is carded.\n\n4. THE ALTERNATES ARE SHADOWED, NOT LOGGED. Every linear row that reached levels and was not carded goes into the shadow book's TESTED payload like any other tested candidate (trade_book_shadow_spec), with \"letter\" = its first failing letter, or \"x\" when it passed every part and another row was carded, and \"reason\" opening \"alt Pnn: \" (the card this view produced) or \"alt none: \" (no row carded), then the theme in 6 words or fewer. Option rows are not shadowed: the shadow book scores stops and targets only, and on FX the R18 twin scores the option. Alternates write no LOG T line and no TESTED line of their own, which keeps the trade document inside its cap. The weekly review compares each card with its alternates from these tags.\n\n5. VIEW STANDS. A lean whose view passes (d) and (e) while every row fails (c) is a live view that these levels do not pay for. Its TESTED line ends \"not carded (c): view stands, <the number that fails, 5 words at most>\", so that he reads it as a view to structure himself and not as a rejected idea.\n\n6. PRINT. Under the theme's \"My read & lean\", for each view with two or more rows: the word \"EXPRESSIONS\", then one line per row of 22 words at most, \"(n) <trade phrase> via <proxy> · r/r <x.x> · p <nn%> vs <p0%> · EV <±x.xxR> · <Pnn / passes, not chosen / fails (letter): 5 words at most>\". The trade block at the top is unchanged: its TESTED list and the LOG still carry one line per lean, for the row that was carded or, with none carded, for row (1); the footer's \"tested n\" counts leans, not rows.\n\n7. LOAD. Tables for at most 3 views a day, in theme order; the other live views are tested on row (1) alone. If STEP 3E part 2 (new trades) is reached after 07:35 SGT, every lean is tested on row (1) alone that day and the footer's trade-book line says \"expressions: skipped (late run)\". The email is never late for a table.", "rationale": "Owner approved the Takeaways workflow review on 10 Nov 2026 (decision 6): for each theme that survives the view stage print up to four candidate expressions with p, reward-to-risk and EV and card the best; tag the alternates by theme in the shadow book so the weekly review compares the card with what was passed over; read the rejected-idea lines that fail on arithmetic alone as views to structure himself; no change to the gate. Choosing the best of several rows on the model's own p can overstate EV, which is why every alternate is shadowed and the comparison is made weekly before the selection is trusted.", "evidence": "Workflow review, 10 Nov 2026: tested ideas rejected on arithmetic alone moved the lean's way more often than not over the next five sessions, while ideas rejected for no catalyst or as already priced mostly went the other way: the two view tests carry the gate's value and the arithmetic test does not separate winners. As linear shadows at their own stop and target the arithmetic rejections were about flat while the other two groups lost: the levels failed, not the views. Counts and results are in the database row only.", "revert_if": "Revert if, after 6 weeks or 15 cards chosen from a table, the carded rows have not beaten the average of their shadowed alternates in R; or if the tables cost the daily run its 08:15 SGT landing on 2 or more days. Item 3(i) lapses when R18's trial ends.", "supersedes": null, "review_due": "2026-12-22", "source": "owner"}$j$::jsonb);
